# Exp46 — Exit / No-Exit Timing Transport Decomposition — FROZEN

Frozen 2026-08-13 after Exp45 completion and before any Exp46 exit-timing score.

## Scientific question

After accounting for the frozen robust Position core, does the already-frozen `SEMI_SURV` law improve prediction of whether the corridor has exited by the frozen horizon (`EXIT` vs `NO_EXIT`) relative to `POSITION_SURV` across all eight frozen direction×time environments, without refit, recalibration, alternate Dwell transform, or feature addition?

This isolates the complementary WHEN/WHETHER component. It is a predictive factorization test, not a rescue of Exp42/43 and not a claim that full Dwell invariance has been established.

## Frozen predictions and target

Use exact original Exp41 TRAIN-fitted cumulative probabilities unchanged:

```text
p_EXIT_POS(H)  = 1 - P_NO_EXIT_POSITION(H)
p_EXIT_SEMI(H) = 1 - P_NO_EXIT_SEMI(H)

y_exit = 1 if observed label is ADVANCE or RECAPTURE by H
         0 if observed label is NO_EXIT by H
```

All eligible Exp41 state-horizon cells are included. No conditioning on side. No new fit. No recalibration.

## Frozen environments / horizons / estimand

Reuse exactly Exp44/45 joint environments and `15/30/60/120m` horizons.

Primary within each joint environment:

```text
EXIT_STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED pooled across all four horizons
uncertainty = whole-BRT-day bootstrap preserving all eligible cells for environment/day
```

An environment is formally scorable only if both EXIT and NO_EXIT are present and at least two BRT days contribute eligible cells; otherwise `UNDERPOWERED_EXIT_ENVIRONMENT`.

## Frozen formal gate

Compare `p_EXIT_SEMI` vs `p_EXIT_POS` with binary Brier and binary LogLoss.

Required in all 8 joint environments:

```text
gain = loss(POSITION) - loss(SEMI)
CI95 lower bound > 0
```

Thus 16 mandatory proper-score cells.

```text
EXIT_TIMING_DWELL_TRANSPORT=PASS only if all 16 cells pass
ROBUST_WHEN_WHETHER_EXIT_COMPONENT=PASS only if every environment is scorable and all 16 cells pass
```

Even if Exp46 passes, prior Exp42/43 strict multiclass Dwell transport failures remain historical facts; Exp46 would establish only the binary EXIT/NO_EXIT timing component under this frozen decomposition.

## Diagnostics only

```text
EXIT/NO_EXIT counts and rates
horizon-specific point gains
EXIT AUC POSITION->SEMI
binary calibration by environment/horizon
descriptive UP-DOWN and EARLY-LATE gain differences
```

Diagnostics cannot rescue formal inference.

## Anti-rescue

```text
NO alternate EXIT definition
NO conditioning on side
NO horizon subset
NO dropping joint environment
NO side/era-specific fit
NO direction/time interaction
NO recalibration/intercept/threshold
NO alternate Dwell transform or Dwell bucket
NO new feature
NO Exp38/39 or D1/Clock/Z/Fib/weekday/Scale/Energy/HMM context
NO VAL/TEST refit
NO Exp27 scoring/modification
```

Exp46 failure cannot erase Exp40/41, Exp44 ROBUST_POSITION_CORE, or Exp45 ROBUST_WHICH_SIDE_LAW. Historical OOS remains exploratory; runtime promotion NONE.
